From 747ef4157dd0baaaab27cac577d4bfd8d5c7c608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Schaka <jonastanzer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] rocblas: force WorkGroupMapping=1 for gfx803 assembly solutions

WHY
---
wgm-miscompute.sh's own investigation (RX 470, ROCm 6.4.4) found that
gfx803's assembly-kernel WorkGroupMapping!=1 swizzle does not produce a
bijection between workgroups and output tiles, so affected GEMMs silently
return wrong results with rocblas_status_success. That finding is
unchanged here -- this patch is a different mechanism for the same fix,
not a re-investigation.

The sed script rewrites text across Tensile's whole Logic/ yaml tree
(unbounded file count, no fixed location), which it can only do safely
because this image builds exactly one architecture (rmake.py -a gfx803,
per that script's own header) -- in a real multi-architecture build it
would blindly rewrite every other architecture's WorkGroupMapping entries
too. Tensile/SolutionStructs.py's assignDerivedParameters() is the single
normalization pass every solution's parameter dict goes through --
whether freshly generated or loaded from a Logic yaml at build time --
and already does WorkGroupMapping normalization (negative values, -1 ->
1) right above where this patch adds its own gfx803-gated override. Doing
the same fix there instead: a ~15-line diff on one file, reviewable, and
gated on the solution's own ISA tuple so it cannot execute for any other
architecture's solutions, structurally, not just by construction of this
image.

VERIFIED on real gfx803 hardware (RX 470, 192.168.1.214), not just
build-level: an initial same-pin static comparison looked like a
regression (518 "_WGM8" kernel-name occurrences remained in a real
rocblas-builder build's TensileLibrary_Type_*_fallback_gfx803.{hsaco,dat}
files, where wgm-miscompute.sh's sed leaves zero) -- investigated rather
than reverted-and-forgotten. Every one of those 518 kernel names carries
ISA000_KLS (Tensile's HIP-*source* kernel-language marker), not
ISA803_KLA (assembly) -- exactly the kernel class this script's own
header already measured as correct regardless of WGM value ("WGM8 source
kernels: 2/2 correct... the swizzle is emitted by the compiler rather
than by Tensile"). Confirmed directly: rocblas_dgemm
(TensileLibrary_Type_DD_*_fallback) and rocblas_zgemm (..._ZZ_*_fallback)
both correct to ~1e-16 relative error across multiple shapes on real
hardware, and zero "_WGM8" kernels remain anywhere OUTSIDE the fallback
libraries (i.e. the actual ISA803_KLA kernels this patch targets are
clean). This patch is wired into the Dockerfile -- wgm-miscompute.sh
remains in patches/rocblas/ for reference/rollback, not invoked anymore.

Also NOT YET established whether the underlying WGM!=1 assembly-codegen
defect is gfx803-specific or a Tensile bug shared with other GCN-family
architectures (AGENTS.md workflow step 3's differential test hasn't been
run for this bug, on this patch or the sed it's based on). Working
assumption per Schaka: gfx803-specific is the more likely explanation,
since gfx900/gfx906/etc. see far more real-world and AMD-internal CI
exercise than an unsupported-since-6.0 architecture, and a GEMM
correctness bug this blunt (any assembly kernel with WGM!=1, not a narrow
shape/dtype corner) would plausibly already have surfaced there if it
were architecture-general. Plausible, not confirmed.

WHAT
----
Immediately after assignDerivedParameters()'s existing WorkGroupMapping
normalization (the `if state["WorkGroupMapping"] == -1: ... = 1` block),
force WorkGroupMapping=1 whenever the solution's ISA is gfx803 (8, 0, 3)
and its KernelLanguage is Assembly -- the exact scope wgm-miscompute.sh's
own measurements cover (WGM8 assembly kernels 0/14 correct; WGM8 source
kernels 2/2 correct, so HIP-source kernels are left untouched here, unlike
the sed which also rewrote their (harmless) WGM entries).

Applies to: Tensile @ rocm-libraries commit
cd9574023093742434e8c992d13b89ab9a6c1cf8 (therock-7.14 / ROCm 7.14.0
pin), same commit wgm-miscompute.sh already targets in this line.
---
diff --git a/shared/tensile/Tensile/SolutionStructs.py b/shared/tensile/Tensile/SolutionStructs.py
index e4a0457e70..92a941813d 100644
--- a/shared/tensile/Tensile/SolutionStructs.py
+++ b/shared/tensile/Tensile/SolutionStructs.py
@@ -3210,6 +3210,21 @@ class Solution(collections.abc.Mapping):
       # -1 code is same as 1. Convert to 1.
       state["WorkGroupMapping" ] = 1

+    # GFX803_WGM_MISCOMPUTE_PATCH: on gfx803 (GCN3/Polaris), the assembly
+    # kernel's WorkGroupMapping!=1 swizzle (blockId = wg1 / WGM, then a
+    # magic-number-divide re-deal across a WGM-wide tile block) does not
+    # produce a bijection between workgroups and output tiles -- several
+    # workgroups land on the same tile while others are never claimed, so
+    # the GEMM silently returns wrong results with rocblas_status_success.
+    # WGM only ever permutes which workgroup claims which tile (the grid
+    # and tile set are unchanged), so WorkGroupMapping=1 (identity) is
+    # always a valid, correct assignment -- forcing it here costs some L2
+    # locality on large GEMMs and nothing else. See
+    # patches/rocblas/wgm-miscompute.sh for the hardware measurements
+    # this is based on.
+    if tuple(state["ISA"]) == (8, 0, 3) and state["KernelLanguage"] == "Assembly":
+      state["WorkGroupMapping" ] = 1
+
     # avoid bug somehow related to GlobalSplitU + Persistent
     # avoid bug related to WGM<0
     # General Batch doesn't support PersistentKernel
